    "turn_text": "I think we're dealing with one of the one of the topics I've been talking about for a long time and I get to get into the book as well as We're in a new Cold War with the Chinese government, and the battlefield is over advanced technology. And the only way America is going to win is if the public and the private sector are working together. So being able to work on these issues now, I'm on the board of a company called OpenAI. They are developing artificial general intelligence, meaning you're going to have an algorithm. That is better at a thing than most humans. This isn't science fiction anymore. This is science reality, right? Coders are using this now in order to develop code. It's like 30% of the code that's on GitHub is developed using this tool. We can program DNA the way we program computer code now. There's a biotechnology company we're helping with. I don't know if you've ever eaten an impossible burger, an impossible burger. Tastes like meat because some scientists figured out it's hemoglobin that makes blood, that makes meat taste like meat. And so they took the hemoglobin and injected it into a yeast molecule and made the yeast molecule bleed. You're like, what the heck, right? So for me, the opportunity. to use all those things I've learned, you know, when I was in the CIA, when I was in cybersecurity company, when I was in Congress to work on this cutting edge. So that's been great. And I, and I work at a company called Allen and company and managing director. where I'm advising all kinds of technology companies that have a national security application. So it's been a lot of fun. So brother's been busy. And that's what you're saying. The brother's been busy. He's making bank. He's sort of creating that nexus between his CIA world, his congressional world and his business world, which is all good. Now, you know, I get the, you know, Hima globin into yeast, but you know, Dude, I just kept the cow up, grind that meat down, baby, and s